title ALES173 — Lotus's stereo_notch: the band-reject carried into stereo, the SAME two cutoffs on BOTH channels, each channel a stateless parallel sum — the fourth rung of the stereo EQ / filter class
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES172: take the next agent-doable crux Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES172 carried the band-pass into stereo (keep the middle). Its exact complement is the band-reject — the notch (keep the edges, drop the middle): the surgical cut for mains hum, a resonant ring, mud. Its mono form (notch.rye, ALES47) sums, in parallel, a low-pass at the low cutoff and a high-pass at the high cutoff, saturated once. The natural fourth rung of the stereo EQ class, the band-pass's mirror.
think Unlike ALES172's stateful band-pass and like ALES171's stateless shelf, the notch runs fresh filters over the whole span each call — no carried state. So composed stereo_notch as a stateless free function mirroring stereo_shelf: StereoNotchError = tone.ToneError reused whole; validate BOTH cutoffs + span once against the shared length before either channel writes (atomic refusal), then notch.notch on each channel with the same two cutoffs.
think Proved four laws against the real ALES47 tool: stereo notch law (each channel == mono notch byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); zero-width / direct-current law (equal cutoffs the identity on both — the reject band of zero width — a settled constant surviving per channel as the notch keeps DC); complement law (the notch is neither the input, nor a plain low-pass, nor a plain high-pass, nor ALES172's band-pass on the same cutoffs — keep the edges, not the middle); image/balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (identical-channel master stays identical, three refusals each leaving both channels untouched and balanced).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME clean (opening triad, ≥2 asserts/fn with // invariant, no @memcpy, named errors with try, i64 sum-then-clamp-once per channel). Fourth EQ rung landed; the stereo EQ class now holds tone, shelf, band-pass, and notch — the band-pass/notch complement pair whole.
